 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your new road has to cross a creek. A bridge is expensive, so you just fill it with dirt.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Truckload after truckload, until the road runs straight across. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the creek still has to go somewhere. It piles up behind your road.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "When it rains, the water climbs to the top and pours over the asphalt.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water running over loose dirt is a disaster. In one night, your road washes away.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you rebuild it with a big pipe at the bottom. That's called a culvert.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The creek flows through the pipe, and the road stays dry on top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Until autumn. Leaves and branches wash downstream and plug the pipe.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The water rises again, and you're right back where you started.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So this time, you size it for the biggest storm in a hundred years, not a normal day.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "A wide concrete box lets branches slide right through.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the water shoots out fast, so you line the exit with heavy rocks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Otherwise it would dig a hole right under the end of your road.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a culvert. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
